        "Updated on 04/09/2025 to include hasCategoricalCollection." ,
        "Updated on 27/08/2025 to add source information and skos:description. Previous version did not include these fields." ;
    skos:inScheme cs: ;
    skos:prefLabel "conservation status jurisdiction"@en ;
    skos:skopeNote "Conservation status jurisdiction refers to the different government bodies, such as national, state, or territory, which can differ between levels of government and thir specific legislation. While the IUCN provides global standards, Australia uses a Common Assessment Method (CAM) to align national and state-based assessments, with each jurisdiction responsible for assessing and listing species within its own legal framework." ;
